  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thanks! Try to look up at the clouds once in a while, officer.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Good luck. I hope you find something beautiful in all this gray.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019ll see you in the next dream. Sleep well."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - A room all to myself? Maybe I can finally finish my poem.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "It\u2019s very quiet in here. I think I can hear the building breathing."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - A cage is just a perspective. My mind is still outside.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Wait... I wasn't... finished... with the first chapter...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Everything is... fading to... a very... soft white...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Finally... I can... fly... away...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - "A room of my own? Maybe I\u2019ll finally get to the chapter I\u2019ve been
    putting off."
  - Isolation sounds like the title of a poem I've been meaning to write.
  - The walls in here have such a particular texture. Very honest.
  killExitLines:
  - "I had so many more pages\u2026 left in the chapter\u2026"
  - "Strange\u2026 it feels just like\u2026 the end of a long book\u2026"
  - "I hope someone\u2026 tends the plants\u2026 on my windowsill\u2026"
