  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1784f41e142caf249b19b0222a3656d3, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The police precinct. I'm off duty.
    midDaysAnswer: I was helping with crowd management near the south gate.
    finalDaysAnswer: Patrol. Fewer of us doing it now. Someone has to.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The garage. Long shift. My hands are still dirty. Didn't
      have time to clean up.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I needed some time. Haven't been to the precinct
      in a few days.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nowhere. I've been on the roof watching the sky. No
      patrol. Nobody asked for one.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing out of the ordinary. I stay in good condition.
    midDaysAnswer: My reflexes feel slower. It worries me more than I let on.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't sleep well. But that's been true for years.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My reflexes have been off. I've been concerned about
      it. Didn't want to say anything at the precinct.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Reflexes are fine. Sharp as ever. I condition every morning.
      Nothing wrong with me.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I sleep wonderfully. Long, deep, dreamless. Better than
      I can remember. Genuinely better.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My partner, Irakli. We've been together six years.
    midDaysAnswer: My partner. He works nights now, so we barely see each other.
    finalDaysAnswer: My partner. We don't talk much. We're both tired.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I live alone. Always have. It's cleaner that
      way.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My partner and I are on the same schedule now. We see
      each other all the time. It's good.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Alone. Haven't had a partner in years. Better for the
      work, honestly.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - "Sorry \u2014 I was miles away. The light on the rooftops this morning was
      extraordinary."
    - Do you ever feel like we are all just characters in a very long novel?
    - I was watching the river on the way here. The smog gives it this incredible
      amber color.
    midDays:
    - I found a flower growing through the crack in the pavement today. It looked
      so brave.
    - People are moving so fast they are missing how quiet the city has become.
    - I forgot to fill in the date. Time feels a bit optional lately, does it not?
    finalDays:
    - I am going to the rooftop tonight. I want to see if the stars look different
      from up there.
    - The world is just shedding its skin. We will see what is underneath soon.
    - I almost do not recognize myself in the windows anymore. I find that interesting
      rather than frightening.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
